-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",297,{
[9473]="7003794A\n1\tFind a member of the Reeve's family\tSomeone must have survived the attack on the Mead Hall. An advisor of the Reeve or a family member should be somewhere inside Woodhurst, in the north-west corner of the Stonedeans.\n2\tTalk to Elda\tElda is near the Mead Hall in Woodhurst. Arnwi asked you to speak with Elda, another of the Reeve's advisors.\n3\tReturn to Arnwi near the stable\tArnwi is standing near the stable-master of Woodhurst. Elda refused to speak with you and told you to return to Arnwi.\n4\tTalk to Calin\tCalin is in the farm-house on the eastern side of Woodhurst. Arnwi suggested that you speak next with the third advisor, Calin.\n",
[9474]="70030B2F\n1\tVenture north-west into Fangorn\tYou should head to the northernmost parts of Fangorn to see what can be seen there.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have encountered a very distressed Huorn, trapped in a great tangle of sticky and cruel webs. He stands at the base of a stone stair, and you do not much like the feeling of this place.\n",
[9475]="70030434\n1\tFind the Thane of Floodwend\tThe city of Floodwend is in the south-eastern part of the Wold, but the road is said to be treacherous. You should travel to the Wold and search for the Thane there.\n",
[9476]="700265A8\n1\tDefeat Angmarim look-outs (total: 4)\tAngmarim look-outs can be found within the ruins of Annúminas. Orchalwë is desperate to defeat the Angmarim in Annúminas.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will be pleased to hear the look-outs have been removed.\n",
[9477]="7004A39F\n1\tContinue searching for Captain Lachír\tThe first soldiers left behind saw Captain Lachír and his party heading east along the central road of Udûn, before turning north. You should continue to search for Captain Lachír.\n2\tTalk to the soldiers\tThe soldiers are just north of the central road in Udûn. You should talk to this second set of soldiers and see what you can learn of Captain Lachír.\n3\tOpen hatchways (total: 6)\tThe soldiers are just north of the central road in Udûn. Othras and his fellow-soldier asked for your help in opening hatchways in their area, in search of artifacts or treasure.\n4\tTalk to Mellor\tThe soldiers are just north of the central road in Udûn. You should tell Mellor and Othras that these hatchways are not full of treasure - only belligerent forge-workers!\n5\tTalk to Othras\tThe soldiers are just north of the central road in Udûn. You should encourage the soldiers to stop opening the hatchways.\n6\tClose opened hatchways (total: 4)\tThe soldiers are just north of the central road in Udûn. With permission to abandon their mad task, the soldiers have asked you to help by closing some of the hatchways again.\n7\tTalk to Othras\tThe soldiers are just north of the central road in Udûn. Now that a number of the hatchways have been closed again, you should return to the soldiers.\n",
[9478]="7001487A\n1\tThrow levers (total: 2)\tThe bridge is very near the fallen rucksack and book of the dwarf who fell to his death. You should throw the levers on the bridge to open the waterway running from the Dwarf-Lord's Gate to the Dolven-view.\n2\tThe bridge lies to the north of the Dolven-view.\t\n3\tTalk to Wafri at the Dolven-view camp\tWafri is at the Dolven-view camp, south of the bridge. You should return to Wafri and inform him that, even though you threw all the levers, you did not hear any water flow through the ancient waterways.\n",
[9479]="700687B6\n1\tTûphik has asked you to give Xêrba drink samples to wandering citizens so you can get their opinions. You can find them around the gardens outside The Din of Arms.\t\n2\tTalk to Tûphik at The Din of Arms\tYou have no more samples of Xêrba to give! You should report back to Tûphik at The Din of Arms.\n",
[9480]="7004455A\n1\tLook for suspicious characters throughout the city and confront them. They could be anywhere!\t\n2\tReturn the stolen goods\tReturn the stolen goods retrieved from the thieves to Húrin.\n",
[9481]="70001712\n1\tTalk to Branan\tBranan is by the gate of the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro, among the hills of Fasach-falroid. Búdan has sent you to find a Man named Branan in the city of Donnvail in an attempt to cast off the oppressive yoke of Angmar.\n",
[9482]="7001CD5B\n1\tDefeat bog-lurkers in the Arboretum (total: 8)\tOnce noble guardians of the forest, the bog-lurkers in the Arboretum of Garth Agarwen are now twisted and terrible creatures thriving on blood. They must be slain for they cannot be saved.\n",
[9483]="7001D01A\n1\tDefeat Créoth (total: 18)\tCréoth watch the entrance to the barrow of Garth Agarwen at the behest of the Gaunt Lord, Ivar. They are the first line of defence and a formidable opponent. These Men, loyal to the corrupt being that their ancestors helped to create, are without conscience and filled with malice. Their redemption is unlikely, and it falls to you, in this place, to defeat them.\n",
[9484]="7001E5E4\n1\tDefeat Créoth Hillmen within the Garth Agarwen fortress (total: 40)\tYou should hunt through the fortress and the ruins for the Créoth Hillmen. Purge the true-blooded minions of Angmar and punish them for defiling the natural order in the Lone-lands.\n",
[9485]="7001CD59\n1\tDefeat darkwater in the Arboretum (total: 12)\tTerrifying foes of ancient times, the darkwater use water to form themselves into horrible creatures of darkness. They do not suffer the living and must be destroyed wherever they are found.\n",
[9486]="7001E5E5\n1\tDefeat darkwater within the Garth Agarwen fortress (total: 7)\030Defeat Raugzdrok\tYou should force the darkwater from their hiding places within the pool of the Garth Agarwen fortress and confront their master, Raugzdrok.\n",
[9487]="7001D01B\n1\tDefeat the decayed (total: 18)\tDecayed can be found within unlikely locations, lurking in the crevasses and darkness of stone corridors throughout the barrows. Exposing these creations will require you to spring their trap, but do not be surprised; keep your wits about you, and you will destroy these vile creations.\n",
[9488]="7001CD5A\n1\tDiscover the Memorial of Nailion\030Discover the Stone of Mingond\030Discover Fuirvaw's resting place\030Discover Hargam's resting place\030Discover Halvegil's resting place\tThe Garth Agarwen Arboretum was home to many important locations. These included the tombs of three of their champions: Fuirvaw, Hargram, and Halvegil, a statue to their first king, Nailion, and the founding stone that served as the marker for the bounds of their land: the Stone of Mingond.\n",
[9489]="7001D01C\n1\tDiscover the first unmarked tomb\030Discover the second unmarked tomb\030Discover the third unmarked tomb\030Discover the fourth unmarked tomb\030Discover the fifth unmarked tomb\tThough the Rhudaur fell quickly, they had heroes, and not all the Rhudaur were part of the malignancy that crept into the land. There are five such heroes entombed within the Garth Agarwen barrows. You should visit their graves. If for no other reason than to know that these Men were not the culprits behind the great tragedy of this land.\n",
[9490]="7001CD5C\n1\tDefeat wights in the Arboretum (total: 9)\tWights within the Arboretum continue to spread corruption to the flora and fauna in the area. To begin healing the land these foul creatures must be cut out of the world.\n",
[9491]="7001D01D\n1\tDefeat wights (total: 30)\tWights patrol the befouled land in an endless journey through the mire. They wait until they will be called on by their dread lord, Ivar, to make war upon the living and began their campaign of corruption through the land. It need not be this way. Armed as you are, you can aid the Free Peoples of the world by ridding the land of these foul creatures.\n",
[9492]="7001E5E6\n1\tDefeat wights within the Garth Agarwen fortress (total: 25)\tYou should cleanse the ruins of Garth Agarwen of the wights who have so long stood a vigil over the continued corruption of the land. With them removed, perhaps healing can begin within the swamp of Agamaur.\n",
[9493]="7000ACE4\n1\tBring Orc Battle-medallions to Nethúr at Esteldín.\030Collect Orc battle-medallions (total: 10)\tOrcs can be found in Dol Dínen, south-east of Esteldín, in the North Downs. Nethúr is at Esteldín. Nethúr asked you to collect Orc battle-medallions and bring them to her.\n",
[9494]="7000ACE6\n1\tBring Orc Campaign-medallions to Nethúr at Esteldín.\030Collect Orc campaign-medallions (total: 10)\tOrcs can be found in Malenhad, far to the north of Esteldín, in Angmar. Nethúr is in Esteldín. Nethúr has asked you to collect the campaign medallions of Angmar's cunning Orcs and bring them to her.\n",
[9495]="7000828C\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Meluinen (total: 10)\tOrc-scouts have crept into Meluinen from the valley to the south-west of Lin Giliath. Brethilwen has asked you to slay any Orcs you find in Meluinen, thus reducing the Ongbúrz threat.\n2\tTalk to Brethilwen\tBrethilwen is in Lin Giliath. Brethilwen will be heartened to hear of your victory over the Orcs that had entered Meluinen.\n",
[9496]="7001B1CE\n1\tDefeat Tarkrîp grunts (total: 5)\030Defeat Tarkrîp prowlers (total: 5)\030Defeat Tarkrîp killers (total: 3)\tOrc-encampments can be found north and east of the Old Greenway Fort. Andreg asked you to make your way north to strike against the Orcs trickling in from the North Downs.\n2\tTalk to Andreg at the Old Greenway Fort\tAndreg is at his post outside of the Old Greenway Fort. Orcs crawling throughout the hills north of the Old Greenway Fort seem to be larger in number than the Rangers previously thought. Andreg must be informed.\n",
[9497]="70041AED\n1\tDefeat Orkish forces in Gríshru (total: 12)\tOrkish forces can be found in the encampment of Gríshru. You should defeat Orkish forces.\n2\tSpeak with Laerind\tLaerind is in the village of Ethring. You should speak with Laerind.\n",
[9498]="7001BFA3\n1\tDefeat Gnâshrakh\tThe Orc-leader Gnâshrakh is within Iorvinas. Henir advised that you not waste the opportunity to find the Orc-leader and put an end to him. One fewer Orc in the world is a good thing, and one fewer leader among the Orcs is a great thing.\n2\tTalk to Henir at the entrance to Iorvinas\tHenir is at the entrance to the ruins of Iorvinas. Defeating the Orc-leader proved simple enough. Henir will be pleased to know that you have carried out the duty he placed before you.\n",
[9499]="70033320\n1\tDestroy Orc-barriers (total: 6)\tOrc-barriers can be found throughout the Crack's Edge in the centre of Nud-melek. You should destroy Orc-barriers.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed several Orc-barriers at the Crack's Edge camp.\n",
[9500]="700082EB\n1\tDefeat Orcs (total: 15)\tThe Orcs threatening the central North Downs can be found around the farm fields and rolling hills of Kingsfell. You should foray against the Orcs, and drive them away.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have assisted the Rangers of Esteldín in their daily vigilance, maintaining that the lands of the North Downs are free from enemy control.\n",
[9501]="70027255\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the South Gravenwood (total: 10)\tAndreg asked you to help him hunt Orcs in the South Gravenwood.\n2\tTalk to Andreg\tYou should speak with Andreg regarding your successes against the Orcs of the White Hand in the South Gravenwood.\n",
[9502]="70000757\n1\tDefeat Tarkrîp grunts (total: 5)\030Defeat Tarkrîp prowlers (total: 5)\030Defeat Tarkrîp killer\tThe Orcs are encamped north along the Greenway and wander along the countryside. Saeradan requires your help dealing a telling blow against the Orcs from the north. The more Orcs slain, the better the chances that an alliance between the brigands and the Orcs will be ineffectual.\n2\tTalk to Saeradan\tSaeradan's cabin is on a wooded hill east of Thornley's farm. Your venture has met with success. You should report back to Saeradan.\n",
[9503]="70000706\n1\tBring Candaith's bow to Candaith\030Collect Candaith's bow\tWhite Hand archers scout the Midgewater Pass, and can be found also within Bleakrift, north-west of Candaith's camp at the foot of Weathertop. Candaith has asked you to recover his bow from the archer that has taken it.\n",
[9504]="70026304\n1\tAid Orchalwë with Untoward Aggression\030Aid Orchalwë with Monuments of Angmar\030Aid Orchalwë with Drowning at the Docks\tOrchalwë has decided to join the fight and help to reclaim Annúminas. If you become separated from Orchalwë, you can use the smoke signal he gave you to call him to you.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will want to discuss all that has happened.\n3\tTalk to Adadhrond\tAdadhrond is at Echad Garthadir in Annúminas. Adadhrond will want a report of how things went with Orchalwë.\n",
})
